\pard\sa120\sb120\fs32\b Get-OneViewServerList\b0{\*\bkmkstart get-oneviewserverlist}{\*\bkmkend get-oneviewserverlist}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Description\b0{\*\bkmkstart description}{\*\bkmkend description}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Queries GET /rest/server-hardware across all pages and returns a normalised list of servers (name, serial, model, power state, health, iLO IP, enclosure). Each server also reports its HPE OneView maintenance mode (InMaintenance / Operational) from the server-hardware resource's MaintenanceModeEnabled flag. Supports an optional -Filter to narrow the result by health, power state, maintenance mode, or name (substring/wildcard match).\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Parameters\b0{\*\bkmkstart parameters}{\*\bkmkend parameters}\par
\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Parameter\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Description\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -OneViewHost\f0} _(Aliases: -OVHost)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 OneView appliance hostname or IP (e.g. oneview.ad.example.com). If omitted, the command checks for an existing HPEOneView module session (Connect-OVMgmt); when one is active it is reused, otherwise a clean "not connected" status is returned instead of prompting for a host.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Credential\f0} _(Aliases: -Cred)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 PSCredential for authentication. Preferred, non-interactive entry point (sourced from a secret store). Falls back to -OneViewUser/-OneViewPassword or an interactive prompt when omitted. Never read from config or environment.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -OneViewUser\f0} _(Aliases: -OVUser)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 OneView username (used with -OneViewPassword). Never read from config or environment.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -OneViewPassword\f0} _(Aliases: -OVPwd)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 OneView password (used with -OneViewUser). Never read from config or environment.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Port\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 OneView HTTPS port (default 443).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -SkipCertificateCheck\f0} _(Aliases: -SkipCert)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Skip SSL certificate verification for the REST calls that fetch the list. Most OneView appliances in lab/test use a self-signed or internal-CA certificate, so the default is $true. Only relevant while a NEW connection is being established - when an active session is reused it has no effect. Set to $false only against an appliance presenting a fully trusted cert.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -TimeoutSec\f0} _(Aliases: -Timeout)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Per-call timeout (default 30 s) for each paginated REST request. Only relevant while a NEW connection is established or when fetching very large fleets over a slow link; the default is fine for normal use.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -PageSize\f0} _(Aliases: -Page)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Servers fetched per page (default 100, max 1000).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Filter\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Optional client-side filter. Matching is case-insensitive and, by default, a SUBSTRING match, so partial values still match (health:Critical matches "Critical", name:PROD matches "PROD-SRV-01"). The name/power/health values also accept PowerShell-style wildcards: health:<value> e.g. health:Critical, health:\i Warning\i0 power:<value> e.g. power:On, power:Off maintenance:<value> e.g. maintenance:InMaintenance, maintenance:Operational name:<value> e.g. name:PROD (substring), name:PROD-* (wildcard), name:srv-0? (single-char wildcard)\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -MockResult\f0} _(Aliases: -Mock)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Hashtable to return without making any HTTP calls. Used for tests.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -DryRun\f0} _(Aliases: -Dry)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Print the query without performing it.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -PassThru\f0} _(Aliases: -PT)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 By default the command only prints a human-readable table to the terminal and emits NO object to the pipeline (so the console is not cluttered with a raw hashtable/json dump). Pass -PassThru to also return the structured [hashtable] (Success, Count, Servers, Error) for use by scripts or the module Router.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Summary\f0} _(Aliases: -Sum)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Print a condensed table with only Server Name, Serial, MaintMode, Health and iLO IP. Useful for a quick fleet health/maintenance glance. Mutually exclusive in intent with -Detail (default); -Detail is the explicit full-field view.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Detail\f0} _(Aliases: -Det)_\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Print the full table with every field (Server Name, Serial, MaintMode, State, Health, Power, iLO IP, ROM, State Reason, Model). This is the default when neither -Summary nor -Detail is specified.\cell}\row
